        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "712b848e-517a-5cb1-bfbe-521a31cc0bb6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Aloha from Hawaii Via Satellite\n- People: Elvis Presley, Neal S. Blaisdell\n- Places: Honolulu, Hawaii\n- Organizations: City & County of Honolulu\n- Facilities: Neal S. Blaisdell Center, Honolulu International Center\n\nFacts:\n- In 1964, the Neal S. Blaisdell Center in Honolulu, Hawaii was constructed on the historic Ward Estate and was originally called the Honolulu International Center.\n- Neal S. Blaisdell Center was renamed after Honolulu mayor Neal S. Blaisdell, who oversaw its construction.\n- Neal S. Blaisdell Center near downtown Honolulu, Hawaii is a community center for the City & County of Honolulu.\n- On January 14, 1973, Elvis Presley headlined the concert Aloha from Hawaii Via Satellite, which was broadcast live via satellite.\n- Aloha from Hawaii Via Satellite took place at the Honolulu International Center in Honolulu, which is now known as the Neal S. Blaisdell Center.\n- Aloha from Hawaii Via Satellite aired in more than 40 countries across Asia and Europe, where the telecast was received the next day in primetime.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
